  "question": {
    "text": "A copper rod of cross-sectional area A carries a uniform current I through it. At temperature T, if the volume charge density of the rod is $\\rho$, how long will the charges take to travel a distance $\\mathrm{d}$ ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dIpbl",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 \\rho \\mathrm{dA}}{\\mathrm{IT}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wvFQZ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 \\rho \\mathrm{dA}}{\\mathrm{I}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RmODE",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\rho \\mathrm{dA}}{\\mathrm{I}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wi13r",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\rho \\mathrm{dA}}{\\mathrm{IT}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Charge density\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\rho=\\frac{\\text { charge }}{\\text { volume }}=\\frac{q}{A d} \\Rightarrow q=\\rho A d \\\\\n&\\text { Also, } q=I T \\Rightarrow T=\\frac{q}{I}=\\frac{\\rho A d}{I}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
